// LocalOverride.xcconfig — developer-local overrides (NOT committed to git)
//
// First-time setup:
//   cp LocalOverride.xcconfig.template LocalOverride.xcconfig
//   # Then edit LocalOverride.xcconfig and replace YOUR_TEAM_ID with your
//   # Apple Developer Team ID (10-character alphanumeric string).
//   # Find yours at: https://developer.apple.com/account → Membership
//
// This file (LocalOverride.xcconfig) is listed in .gitignore so your
// personal signing identity is never committed.
//
// The template (LocalOverride.xcconfig.template) IS committed so every
// developer on the team gets the setup instructions on a fresh clone.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOUR_TEAM_ID

// ── Kernel entitlements (optional, requires paid Apple Developer account) ──────
//
// Uncomment the line below ONLY after:
//   1. Upgrading to a paid Apple Developer Program account ($99/year)
//   2. Adding "Increased Memory Limit" and "Extended Virtual Addressing"
//      capabilities in Xcode → Signing & Capabilities
//   3. Confirming the provisioning profile includes both entitlements
//
// This unlocks the generous memory tier on iPhone 16 Pro / iPad Pro:
//   - n_ctx up to 4096 tokens (vs 2048 without)
//   - MLX GPU cache up to 128 MB (vs 50 MB without)
//   - Full image token budget (256 vs 70 tokens)
//   - Models > 2 GB load safely (mmap limit lifted)
//
// Without a paid account, leave this commented out (sandboxed mode).
// The app runs correctly with conservative memory limits.
// See KERNEL_ENTITLEMENTS.md for full setup instructions.
//
// SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS = $(inherited) HOMEHUB_HAS_KERNEL_ENTITLEMENTS

// ── Optional: llama.cpp GGUF runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────
// Uncomment BOTH lines when llama.xcframework is placed alongside the repo root.
// See README.md → "Optional: llama.cpp opt-in"
//
// SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS = $(inherited) HOMEHUB_LLAMA_RUNTIME
// GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS = $(inherited) HOMEHUB_LLAMA_RUNTIME=1
